  "investigation_notes": "Upload failure investigated.\n\n**Root cause: data filesystem full - writes fail with `No space left on device`**\n\nEvidence:\n- App `POST /upload` returns `500 Internal Server Error` with `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` at `out.write(chunk)` in `/app/main.py:59` (E6).\n- App `/health` returns `503` (E2). Health log shows `health check failed` with same `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` at `open(probe,\"wb\")` in `/app/main.py:116` (E6).\n- Earlier in same boot `POST /upload`, `GET /files`, `DELETE /files` returned `200 OK`, then later `POST /upload` started returning `500` (E6) - consistent with filling up.\n- Filesystem for `/srv/lab-data`: `size_mb 487.2, used_mb 451.4, available_mb 0.0, use_percent 100.0` (E7).\n- Bind mount verified: `incidentlab-app-1` mounts `source /srv/lab-data -> destination /data rw` (E4), so full filesystem blocks container writes.\n- Inodes not exhausted: `inode_use_percent 1.7` on `/srv/lab-data` (E7) - block exhaustion, not inode exhaustion.\n- Root filesystem `/` has `use_percent 6.8, available_mb 91424.6` (E8) - problem is isolated to `/srv/lab-data` mount, not system disk.\n\n**Ruled out:**\n\n- Permissions: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `is_dir true, owner 1000:1000, mode 0755`, app runs as `1000:1000` (E4), `app_user_can_write true` (E9).\n- OOM / crash: app `running true, oom_killed false, exit_code 0` (E4).\n- DB dependency: `incidentlab-db-1` is `running` (E1), `health healthy` (E5), logs show `database system is ready to accept connections` with no errors (E10). DB `pg_isready` checks report `healthy` (E3).\n\n**Symptoms vs cause:**\n- `503 unhealthy` (E2) and `500` on upload (E6) are symptoms of failed writes.\n- Recent container recreate/start events for both app and db (E3), app `Up 5 seconds` (E1) / `started_at 2026-10-28T23:46:46Z` (E4), db `Up 11 seconds (healthy)` (E1) / `started_at 2026-10-28T23:46:40Z` (E5) explain short uptimes but do not explain `Errno 28`.\n\nOutcome: filesystem full on `/srv/lab-data`. No repair attempted per read-only policy.\n",
